Dear Yanbing,

Indeed, since you are using MacOS the CRAN servers did not yet have enough time to produce the binaries.
On https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/QCA/index.html, I can see most of them on version 3.7 but there are also lagging versions 3.6 (including the MacOS binary). They will eventually go to 3.7 but this might take a couple of more days.

In the meantime, it is possible to install from sources but that requires you to have the development tools installed (something related to Xcode and command line tools, if you are familiar).

Otherwise, the MacOS binaries can still be found here:
https://artifacts.r-hub.io/QCA_3.7.tar.gz-9c805f4def7f47688b5503711f3149e7/

I regularly use rhub to check and compile my sources, but they will erase them in about a week I believe.

Hope this helps,
Adrian

