Dear Max,

Your example is anything but minimal, however still potentially very useful to follow up.
In order to try simplifying it a little bit, I would suggest activating the argument "use.letters" to replace the long condition names with more simple letters.

Before doing that, I might have a very straightforward question by just looking at your script. When deriving the parsimonious solution, I see you have used: neg.out = TRUE

But that is not used for the intermediate solution. The immediate question is: how do you expect the result to contain what you believe should contain, when the intermediate solution uses the parsimonious solution for the presence of the outcome, while you analysed the parsimonious solution for the absence of the outcome...?

Also, could you also paste the intermediate models specific to C21P20 resulted from version 3.6?
I assume you still have those, otherwise how do you know the result in version 3.7 is different?

Best,

Adrian

